# Files owned by the user — fern generate will not overwrite these.
#
# `custom.rs` must live in the directory the generated `[[bin]]` builds from,
# because generated `main.rs` reaches it via `mod custom;`. When the generator
# renames that directory, this path has to move with it — otherwise the file
# survives regeneration while silently dropping out of the build. That is exactly
# what happened on 2026-08-05: this entry still read `cli/athena/custom.rs`, the
# file was duly preserved, and the binary moved to `cli/athena-intelligence-api/`
# and compiled against the generator's 1.6 KB stub instead. It still compiled, so
# nothing failed — the custom commands just stopped existing.
cli/athena-intelligence-api/custom.rs

# CI is never generated. Without this the whole directory is wiped on every
# regeneration — including build-cli.yml, the workflow that builds and releases
# the binaries, and the only thing that would have caught the loss above.
.github/
